<title>USA: TABLE-Intermagnetics Q4 shr $0.06 vs $0.15.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Intermagnetics Q4 shr $0.06 vs $0.15.</headline>
<dateline>LATHAM, N.Y. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>			May 25, 1997		 May 26, 1996</p>
<p> Shr primary     $	 0.06	   $	 0.15</p>
<p> Net			    711		    1,852</p>
<p> Revs			25,647		   27,763</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	12,541		   12,526</p>
<p>12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary     $	 0.21	   $	 0.36(a)</p>
<p> Net			  2,615		    4,427(a)</p>
<p> Revs			90,013		   94,019</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	12,297		   12,322</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: (a)Includes about $905,000 or $0.07 per share after-tax gain on sale of marketable securities.</p>
<p>Primary shares and earnings per share have been adjusted to reflect a 2 percent stock dividend distributed August 22, 1996.</p>
<p>Revenues and profits in the 1996 quarter included the benefits of a one-time revenue item of nearly $1.0 million for the extension of a license on cryogenic refrigeration products.</p>
<p>Full company name is Intermagnetics General Corp.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
